Dotoran of Frontiers made the following changes to 1.3 to make it 1.5:

1: Colors were updated to new MCI format, as well as using the Upper Eight
   colors(the high intensity ones), as well as a change from BLUE to CYAN
   to aid in the readability of text.

2: Maps were redrawn using IBM ANSI Color/Graphics to give the game more
   Visual Appeal.

3: Menus were given ANSI Color treatment as well as the Maps.

4: Prompts cleaned up a bit, instead of continually printing the prompt if
   an unknown command was used.

5: The $ command has changed to give a "Maintenance" menu to any user with
   the Maintenance flag enabled. These commands are available:

      / C - COMPLETELY Restart Game (Kill Players, Wall, and Log)
NEW  /  E - Edit a Players Stats
for <   S - Start Game Over (Only Kill Players & Log, but leave Wall)
1.5  \  L - Start Log  Over (Only Kills the Log)
      \ R - Edit Motel "Reminder" (Using CNet's Editor)

      / P - Play Another of YOUR Aliases    (Was the $ command in 1.3)
OLD  /  A - Add New Player to Motel         (Was the # command in 1.3)
from<   F - Filename Display Toggle On/Off  (Was the . command in 1.3)
1.3  \  K - Kill a Player from Motel        (Undocumented 1.3 Command)
      \ M - Maint Access Toggle On/Off      (Undocumented "E" Command)

Dotoran

Changes from 1.5 to 1.51:

1: Maint Access was checking Access Level 23, instead of 31. (Gives you an idea
   of how old this file is! hehe)

2: Now uses getuser 40, versus 41, so as not to use the HUGE numbers in filenames.

3: Moved the "Motel!" file from the PFILES: path into the DOORS:Motel/ path, as
   well as renaming it to "MurderMotel".

4: File now uses Smart Path technology, so you can store the "Motel/" directory in
   whatever directory you wish!

5: Included a "File_ID.Diz" file for easy uploading into your own bases.

6: Removed the "Path=" line from the "Motel.Config" file.

7: Cleaned up the filenames used for the Rooms (those that were capitalized).
